// sched.kf - bounded concurrency for Koffuster.
//
// Two independent compiler limitations on this KOF build shape everything
// here (see docs/impl-notes.md for the reproduced failures):
//   1. Neither `listOf<Handle<T>>()` nor `new Handle<T>[n]` survives the
//      JVM bytecode verifier, so there is no dynamic-width collection of
//      in-flight handles. The fallback is a fixed set of unrolled batch
//      widths (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), matching the cookbook's proven P5 shape.
//   2. `spawn f(x)` where `x` references any local variable or parameter
//      (of any type, however deeply nested) corrupts the generated
//      bytecode. Only zero-argument spawn targets work. So the dynamic
//      per-request URL cannot be passed as a spawn argument at all - it is
//      routed instead through a small temp file per batch "slot", written
//      synchronously (a plain function call, unaffected by the bug) right
//      before that slot's zero-arg wrapper is spawned.
//
// Slot temp files use fixed names under /tmp (no PID/run-id API was found
// to make them unique - a zero-arg spawn target has no way to read one
// even if it existed, since top-level functions have no closure over the
// caller's locals). Documented limitation: two `koffuster dir` scans
// running at the exact same moment on the same machine could read one
// another's in-flight slot files. A single run is race-free: every slot's
// file is written before any slot in that batch is spawned.

String slotStatusPath(Int slot) {
    return "/tmp/.koffuster_slot_status_" + slot + ".url"
}
String slotBodyPath(Int slot) {
    return "/tmp/.koffuster_slot_body_" + slot + ".url"
}
String headersFilePath() {
    return "/tmp/.koffuster_headers.txt"
}

// Persist the run's packed header string once at startup so the zero-arg
// slot functions below can read it (they cannot receive it as a spawn
// argument - see the file header comment).
Bool writeHeadersFile(String hdrs) {
    Path(headersFilePath()).writeText(hdrs)
    return true
}

// NOTE: `http.status(url, hdrs)` - the two-argument form - was tried and
// triggers the SAME internal compiler frame-crash as the multi-header
// vararg bug (cookbook P1e), reproduced in docs/impl-notes.md. `http.status`
// only takes a bare URL on this build, so status probes cannot carry
// custom headers/UA/cookie/auth at all; only the body-length probe (which
// uses `http.get`, whose two-argument header form does work) can. This is
// a real, disclosed limitation - see docs/requirements-matrix.md.

// -- status-probe zero-arg spawn targets, one per slot -----------------
Int statusSlot0() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(0)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot1() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(1)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot2() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(2)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot3() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(3)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot4() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(4)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot5() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(5)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot6() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(6)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot7() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(7)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot8() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(8)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot9() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(9)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot10() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(10)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot11() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(11)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot12() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(12)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot13() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(13)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot14() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(14)).readText()) }
Int statusSlot15() { return http.status(Path(slotStatusPath(15)).readText()) }

